<article class="env-lemma" id="08PU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08PU">Lemma <span data-tag="08PU">92.4.3</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $\pi $ and $i$ be as in (<a href="/tag/08PR" data-tag="08PR">92.4.0.1</a>). There is a canonical isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  L_{B/A} = L\pi _!(Li^*\Omega _{\mathcal{O}/A}) = L\pi _!(i^*\Omega _{\mathcal{O}/A}) = L\pi _!(\Omega _{\mathcal{O}/A} \otimes _\mathcal {O} \underline{B})  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(B)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For an object $\alpha : P \to B$ of the category $\mathcal{C}$ the module $\Omega _{P/A}$ is a free $P$-module. Thus $\Omega _{\mathcal{O}/A}$ is a flat $\mathcal{O}$-module. Hence $Li^*\Omega _{\mathcal{O}/A} = i^*\Omega _{\mathcal{O}/A}$ is the sheaf of $\underline{B}$-modules which associates to $\alpha : P \to A$ the $B$-module $\Omega _{P/A} \otimes _{P, \alpha } B$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/08PT" data-tag="08PT">92.4.2</a> we see that the right hand side is computed by the value of this sheaf on the standard resolution which is our definition of the left hand side (Definition <a href="/tag/08PN" data-tag="08PN">92.3.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>